Subject: CPMS I03 Semantic Residual and Conformance Formation Justification

@ [justification_uuid] f7aa289c-3c73-4e9d-a215-c49cec6273d1

& [SelectedExactByteIngress] preserves duplicate-key and trailing-data evidence that a pre-parsed Value would erase
& [SelectedLocalRecursiveVisitor] can reuse locked serde machinery while remaining separately testable and avoids adding a second parser without need
& [SelectedIndependentValidator] cross-checks generated schema behavior rather than trusting the derive path that produced it
& [SelectedNoDefaultFeatures] excludes candidate validator HTTP file and TLS surfaces from the dependency graph
& [SelectedExplicitDraft] prevents ambient draft-detection behavior from becoming contract authority
& [SelectedNormalizedFindings] makes proof deterministic without pretending third-party diagnostic wording is stable API
& [SelectedResidualRegistry] prevents syntax success from concealing digest graph replay resource authority and non-capability conditions
& [SelectedApplicabilityKinds] permits duplicate-key byte refusal and output serialization evidence without manufacturing false schema-serde equivalence
& [SelectedFiniteCorpus] provides repeatable positive negative and boundary witnesses while expressly rejecting exhaustive-language claims
& [SelectedOutputFixtureRoute] validates actual serialized Rust output rather than claiming arbitrary input bytes are constructible output states
& [RejectedImplementationNow] protects source preservation SJS dependency audit activation lock and the current goal boundary
